1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:04,054
The dynasty that unified
China lasted fifteen years.

2
00:00:04,384 --> 00:00:08,584
In 221 BCE, Qin conquers
the last of its rivals,

3
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:11,694
and its king becomes the
First Emperor: one script,

4
00:00:11,744 --> 00:00:17,464
one coinage, one set of weights and
measures. He dies eleven years later.

5
00:00:17,514 --> 00:00:22,056
Within a year, the revolts begin,
and by 206 his dynasty is gone.

6
00:00:22,306 --> 00:00:27,226
But the empire it built outlasts it. The
Han that takes over keeps it for about

7
00:00:27,276 --> 00:00:28,385
four hundred years.

8
00:00:28,755 --> 00:00:32,105
Then it happens again. After
centuries of division,

9
00:00:32,155 --> 00:00:37,085
the Sui reunite China, dig the Grand
Canal, and last thirty-seven years.

10
00:00:37,135 --> 00:00:39,900
The Tang that follows lasts
nearly three hundred.

11
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:44,210
Seven thousand years of China, on
one line. It's OpenChronology,

12
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:45,732
and it's free.
